From 155b4b00421180b3f0b8a1159d70085ee8f9335e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 00:28:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09205/11362] Capture the llama-server's stderr: a crash with
 no log is an unanswerable run

The first Qwen3.8-27B arm died after 2 of 39 cells. The harness recorded the
wedge correctly -- props_identity_lost, Connection refused -- and that is all it
could record, because the server was launched with stdout AND stderr to DEVNULL.

A crashed server with no log cannot be classified. Model defect, llama.cpp
incompatibility with a new architecture, OOM, something else -- all identical from
outside. Re-running blind would have reproduced the same non-answer at four hours
a go.

Server output now goes to a file under the run's own scratch directory, one per
port so the two arms cannot overwrite each other.

WHAT IS AND IS NOT KNOWN, stated because 2 cells is not a result:
  KNOWN     Qwen3.8-27B LOADS and serves -- 17,856 MiB resident on GPU 1, healthy
            in 10.0s, a real /completion probe passed. So the GGUF is intact and
            llama.cpp can run the architecture.
  KNOWN     both attempted inductions failed the same way: load_engine
            FileNotFoundError, no importable world_model.py emitted. That is the
            exact failure mode that lost Qwen3.6 the 2026-07-28 bakeoff (18 of 39).
  NOT KNOWN whether that generalises. n=2 on ONE game (tu93), against gemma's
            38/39 across 13 games. Two cells is not evidence.
  NOT KNOWN why the server died on cell 3. That is what this commit fixes.

The two crashed-run cells are set aside rather than deleted -- resume caches by
cell, so leaving them in place would let a crashed run's output stand as data in
the re-run.

The abort-on-arm-failure guard added with the runner worked: it stopped after the
failed arm instead of spending another four hours on gemma to compare against
nothing.
---
 .../experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py     | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
index 32399bfb34..2acc87964f 100644
--- a/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
+++ b/scripts/experiments/experiment_6440_qwen38_generator_h2h_arm.py
@@ -246,7 +246,18 @@ def launch(arm: dict[str, Any], llama_server: Path) -> tuple[subprocess.Popen, d
     env = dict(os.environ, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=str(GPU_INDEX))
     log(f"  launch: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES={GPU_INDEX} {' '.join(args)}")
     t0 = time.time()
-    proc = subprocess.Popen(args, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=env)
+    # CAPTURE the server's stderr instead of discarding it (changed 2026-08-15). The original
+    # sent both streams to DEVNULL. On the first Qwen3.8 run the server died mid-arm and the
+    # harness recorded only `Connection refused` -- a crash with no log is undiagnosable, so the
+    # run could not be classified as a model problem or an infrastructure one, and re-running
+    # blind would have reproduced exactly the same non-answer.
+    srv_log = (
+        Path(os.environ.get("CARNOT_H2H_SERVER_LOG_DIR", "/tmp"))
+        / f"llama_server_{args[args.index('--port') + 1]}.log"
+    )
+    srv_fh = srv_log.open("ab")
+    log(f"  server stderr -> {srv_log}")
+    proc = subprocess.Popen(args, stdout=srv_fh, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, env=env)
     deadline = t0 + 1800
     healthy = False
     while time.time() < deadline:
-- 
